       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 269}, page_content=''),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 270}, page_content='CURRICULUM'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 271}, page_content='MODULE 1- Python:  Basic to Advance \\n-\\nPython Basics:  \\nUnderstanding Problem Solving | Why Python | What is an IDE (Integrated \\nDevelopment Environment) | Installation of Python – Anaconda & Launching of \\nJupiter Notebook | Write your first Python Program \\n \\n-\\nPython’s Variables and Operators:  \\nArithmetic Operators | Assignment Operators | Python Boolean & Logical Operators | \\nPython Comparison Operators | Python Bitwise Operator \\n \\n- Built-in Functions of Python: \\nRound Function & Divmod Function | Isinstance Function & Pow Function  | Input \\nFunction | Int function | Float Function | Len, Min and Max function | Sorted Function \\n| Help function \\n \\n- Control Flow Statements: \\nIf Condition | If else Condition | If-Elif-else Condition| Nested if \\n \\n- Concepts of Loops: \\nWhile Loop | Break & Continue Statements | For Loop & Range Function | Nested \\nLoops in Python \\n \\n- User-Defined Functions in Python: \\nIntroduction & Doc String | Functions Input Arguments | Functions Order of input \\nArguments | Functions Return Statement | Function Variable Number of Input \\nArguments | *args and **kwargs in Function | Lambda function \\n \\n- Python Strings: \\nIntroduction to String | Indexing & Slicing | Methods – strip, lower, upper |  Methods – \\nreplace, split, capitalize | Methods – title, swapcase, find, index | Methods – isalnum, \\nisalpha, isdigit | Methods – isupper, islower, istitle, startswith, endswith | Multiline \\nString & checking of substring in String | Converting String into another Data Type | \\nLoops in string \\n \\n-\\nList in Python:  \\nIntroduction to List | Slicing on List | Indexing on List | Methods - Append, Extend & \\nInsert in List | Methods - Remove, Pop, Clear | Methods – Count, Max, Min | Reverse, \\nIndex Count, Copy | Using Loops in List | Using conditional statement in List \\nAI Engineer Advanced Course \\nCurriculum Outline \\n\\uf0b7 LEVEL 1 :- Programming Fundamentals'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 272}, page_content='Module 2 - Numerical Programming in Python \\n- Unleashing the Power of NumPy: \\nIntroduction to NumPy | Nd Array Object | Data Types | Array Attributes | Array \\nCreation Routines | Array from Existing | Data Array from Numerical Ranges | \\nIndexing & Slicing | Advanced Indexing | Broadcasting | Iterating Over Array | Array \\nManipulation | Binary Operators | String Functions | Mathematical Functions | \\nArithmetic Operations | Statistical Functions | Sort, Search & Counting Functions | \\nByte Swapping | Copies &Views | Matrix Library | Linear Algebra. \\n-\\nTuples in Python:  \\nIntroduction, Concatenation & Nesting | Length, count, index method, indexing & \\nslicing | The tuple() Constructor | Duplicates in tuples | Max, min, unpacking of tuples | \\nConditional statement and loops in tuple \\n \\n- Sets in Python: \\nIntroduction to Set | Methods - add, update, remove, discard, pop, clear, del, union | \\nMethods - intersection_update, intersection, difference_update, difference | Methods - \\nsymmetric_difference_update, symmetric_difference | Methods - issubset, issuperset, \\nissubset | Methods - set(), max, min, copy, loops in sets \\n \\n- Python Dictionary: \\nIntroduction to Dictionary | Methods-, len, dict constructor fromkeys, setdefault | \\nMethods - get, keys, values, items, update | Methods - pop, popitem, del, clear, copy | \\nMethods - Nested Dictionaries, loops in dictionary \\n \\n- Object Oriented Programming: \\nOOPS Basic concept & creating classes | Polymorphism and encapsulation | Types of \\nInheritance – single, multilevel, multiple, hierarchical | Abstraction & decorator | \\nTypes of methods - Class method, static method | Special-magic/dunder method | \\nProperty decorators – getters, setters and deletes \\n \\n- Files Handling: \\nWorking with Files | Reading & writing files | Buffered Read and Write | Other File \\nMethods | Logging & Debugger \\n \\n- Exception Handling: \\nIntroduction | Exception handling with try, except, else, and finally block of code | \\nCustom Exception Handling | List of general use exceptions | Best Practice Exception \\nHandling'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 273}, page_content=\"- Pandas Playbook: Messy to Masterpiece: \\nIntroduction to Pandas | Reading Data From Different File Systems | Data Frame | \\nOperations | Basic Functionality | Reading Data From Different File Systems | Re-\\nIndexing Python | Iteration | Sorting | Working With Text Data Options & \\nCustomization | Indexing & Selecting  | Data Statistical Functions | Windows Functions \\n| Python Pandas - Date Functionality | Time Delta | Categorical Data | Visualization | \\nPython Pandas – Tools \\n \\n- Visualizing Analytics with Matplotlib: \\nIntroduction to Matplotlib | Bar Chart | Scatter Plot | Bar Graph | Histogram | Pie Chart \\n| Stem Plots | Box Vs Whisker Plot | Area Vs Stack Plot | Step Plot | Fill between Plots | \\nSubplot | Savefig | Axis matplotlib plots | Text in matplotlib plots \\n \\n- Statistical Data Visualization with Seaborn:  \\nIntroduction to Seaborn | Heatmap plot method | Count plot method | Violin Plot \\nmethod | Pair plot method | Strip Plot method | Box plot method | Factor plot method | \\nCat Plot method | Styling plot method | Facet Grid Method | Line Plot method | \\nHistogram plot method | Bar plot method | Scatter plot method \\n \\n- Interactive Data Visualization with Plotly: \\nIntroduction to Plotly | Bubble Charts | Bar Charts | Pie Charts | Creating Maps | Time \\nSeries \\nProjects in Python  \\nPROJECT 01 \\n- Google Image Scrapping with Flask: \\nThis project features a full-stack automated image retrieval tool. Designed to \\nstreamline data collection, the application programmatically queries Google Images, \\nretrieves responsive HTML, and parses the document structure via BeautifulSoup to \\nextract direct asset URLs. The project highlights a practical application of web scraping \\nmethodologies, backend route management, and data pipeline structuring. \\nPROJECT 02 \\n- WhatsApp Chats Analysis: \\nWhatsApp's widespread adoption makes its conversational data an excellent resource \\nfor behavioral and textual analysis. This project explores chat logs to uncover key \\nbehavioral metrics, communication frequency, and sentiment trends across diverse \\nuser interactions, including personal, professional, and group chats. \\nPROJECT 03 \\n- Covid-19 Impacts Analysis: \\nA data-driven analysis of the COVID-19 pandemic’s global footprint, focusing on the \\nrelationship between public health trends and macroeconomic impacts. This project \\nmodels the spread of the virus to evaluate its short- and long-term effects on global \\nmarkets, supply chains, and economic stability.\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 274}, page_content='PROJECT 04 \\n- Movie-Recommendation System: \\nRecommendation engines represent one of the most commercially successful and \\nwidely deployed applications of modern AI Engineering Field. This project focuses on \\ndesigning and implementing an advanced movie recommendation system engineered \\nto analyze viewer preferences and deliver highly accurate, personalized content \\nsuggestions. \\nPROJECT 05 \\n- Smart Price Comparison Tool: \\nThis project focuses on architecting a Python-based data aggregator that evaluates and \\ncompares product metrics across multiple e-commerce datasets. Developers will \\nimplement robust data ingestion pipelines, design data-cleansing algorithms to \\nnormalize disparate product details, and build conditional logic to extract optimal \\nmarket deals. This project provides hands-on experience in ETL (Extract, Transform, \\nLoad) workflows, data normalization, and e-commerce automation—critical skills for \\nmodern data engineering and retail analytics roles. \\nModule 3 – API’s and Real-World Prompting \\n- Foundational Understanding of AI: \\nWhat is Artificial Intelligence and its limitation | Difference between AI, ML, Deep \\nLearning | How AI is trained (Training data, Fine tuning, RL) | Generative AI explained \\nand basic Terminologies | How large language models work | Technology Powering \\nToday’s Smart AI Assistants | Real world AI use cases \\n-\\nMastering Prompt Engineering  and  Advanced Prompting: \\nThe Journey of a Prompt Inside an LLM | Introduction to AI Interaction and Prompt | \\nDesign | The Anatomy of a Perfect Prompt | The Art of Writing High | Impact Prompts \\nUsing Proven Prompting Approaches | Strategic Prompting for Better AI Responses | \\nModifiers for Better Outputs | Types of Prompts | RNN, LSTM and Context Window \\nUnderstanding | Direct Prompting & Token Optimization \\n \\nStructured Prompting & AI Hallucinations | Prompt Priming & Role Based Prompting \\nOutput Formatting control | Zero Shot, Few Shot & Chain of Thought (CoT) | \\nInstruction Prompting & API Parameters | ReAct Framework & Tree of Thoughts \\n(ToT) | Perspective & Comparative Prompting | Tabular Format & Constructive Critic \\nPrompting | Directional Stimulus & Iterative Development | RAG (Retrieval | \\nAugmented Generation) | Use Case: Writing & Content Creation | Use Case: Coding & \\nTechnical Tasks | Use Case: Data Analysis & Business Strategy | Use Case: Dynamic \\nMock Interviewer.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 275}, page_content='Module 4 – Database Management & ETL \\n-\\nIntroduction and Installation Software with Roadmap: \\nDownload & Install MySQL | Download & Install XAMPP | Download & Install \\nPostgreSQL & Pgadmin | Introduction to SQL | Database Fundamental | Learning \\nResources - (Cheat Code | Practice Dataset | PDF Notes & Books | Learning Website | \\nInterview Questions) \\n \\n-\\nCase Study with Example: \\nCreate Database | Drop Database | Create Table | Insert Table | Drop Table | Case study \\nwith XAMPP Software | Case study with MySQL software | Case study with PostgreSQL \\n \\n-\\nData Types and Keys: \\nAll Data Type in SQLs | ER / Database Diagram Example: Amazon Ecommerce | \\nDatabase Keys | Cardinality of Relationships \\n \\n-\\nDDL Commands for SQL: \\nDDL Commands for Databases: Create | Drop | DDL Commands for Table: Create | \\nTruncate | Drop | Data Integrity \\n \\n-\\nConstraints: \\nConstraints in MySQL (NOT NULL | UNIQUE | PRIMARY KEY) | Constraints in MySQL \\n(AUTO INCRIMENT | CHECK | DEFAULT | FOREIGN KEY) | Referential Actions \\n(Restrict | CASCADE | SET NULL | SET DEFAULT) \\n \\n-\\nAlter Table: \\nADD Columns in Alter Table | DELETE Columns in Alter Table | MODIFY Columns in \\nAlter Table \\n \\n-\\nADD, Editing and Deleting Constraints: \\nADD Constraints | DELETE Constraints | EDIT Problems in MySQL, Drop Constraints \\n \\n-\\nINSERT Query: \\nINSERT query | INSERT query variation | INSERT multiple values \\n \\n-\\nSELECT Query: \\nSELECT all columns | Filter columns | Alias | renaming columns | Create expression \\nusing columns | Constant value | DISTINCT(unique) values from a column | DISTINCT \\ncombinations | Filter rows WHERE claus | BETWEEN operator | IN and NOT IN \\nOperator \\n \\n-\\nUPDATE Query: \\nUpdate Query to update row(s) | Update Multiple Columns \\n \\n-\\nDELETE: \\nDELETE Query to delete row(s) | Deletion based on multiple conditions \\n \\n-\\nAggregate Functions: \\nMAX() & MIN() | AVG() | SUM()'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 276}, page_content='-\\nScalar Functions: \\nABS() | ROUND() | CEIL() & FLOOR() \\n \\n-\\nSQL Joins: \\nWhat are SQL Joins? | Types of Joins | Cross Joins --- Cartesian Products | Inner Joins | \\nRight Joins | Left Joins | Full Outer Join | Set Operations | Self-Join | Filtering Columns |  \\nFiltering Rows \\n \\n-\\nSubquery: \\nWhat is Subquery? | Scalar Subquery | Row Subquery | Table Subquery | Correlated \\nSubquery \\n \\n-\\nSorting: \\nFundamental of SQL Sorting | Sorting top 10 data | Sorting Descending Orders | Sorting \\nfunctions in datasets \\n \\n-\\nGrouping: \\nFundamental of SQL Grouping | Grouping Average Function | Group By on multiple \\ncolumns | Sorting Descending Orders | Sorting functions in datasets \\nPROJECT & CASE STUDY \\n- Indian Premier League (IPL Dataset): \\nCase Study in Indian Premier League  \\nFind the top 5 batsmen in IPL  \\nFind the 2nd highest 6 hitters in IPL  \\nFind Batsman (M.S Dhoni, Virat Kohli) performance against all IPL team  \\nFind the top 10 batsmen with centuries in IPL using Sub-Quires  \\nFind the top 5 batsmen with the highest strike rate \\nPROJECT & CASE STUDY \\n- Shipping E-Commerce (Sorting: Smart Phone Datasets): \\nFind the top 5 Samsung phones with the biggest screen size \\nSort all the phones in descending order of the number of total cameras \\nSort data on the basis of ppi in decreasing order \\nFind the phone with 2nd largest battery \\nFind the name and rating of the worst rated apple phone \\nSort phones alphabetically and then on the basis of rating in desc order \\nSort phones alphabetically and then on the basis of price in ascending order \\nPROJECT & CASE STUDY \\n- Music Store Analysis: \\nIn this project, you will work with a music store database to practice SQL queries. It \\nincludes tasks like retrieving customer details, analyzing sales records, and tracking \\npopular tracks and artists. You will also learn how to apply joins, aggregate functions, \\nand filtering to extract meaningful insights. This project strengthens SQL skills \\nthrough real-world data analysis.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 277}, page_content='Module 5 – Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) \\n-\\nEDA With Red Wine Data: \\nExploratory Data Analysis (EDA) With Red Wine Data\" is focusing on the analysis of a \\ndataset related to red wine. Through statistical and visual techniques, this aims to \\nuncover patterns, trends, and insights within the data. \\n \\n-\\nEDA Student Performance Indicator: \\nEDA Student Performance Indicator involves conducting Exploratory Data Analysis \\n(EDA) on a dataset related to student performance. \\n \\n-\\nEDA Forest Fires: \\nEDA Forest Fires refers to an Exploratory Data Analysis project focusing on the \\nexamination of a dataset related to forest fires. \\n \\n-\\nEDA Flight Price: \\nEDA Flight Price focuses on Exploratory Data Analysis for a dataset related to flight \\nprices. \\n \\n-\\nEDA Google Playstore: \\nEDA Google Playstore\" involves conducting Exploratory Data Analysis on a dataset \\nrelated to the Google Play Store.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 278}, page_content='MODULE 6 – Numerical Matrix & Statistics \\n\\uf0b7 LEVEL 2 :- Applied ML Engineering \\n-\\nUNIT 1: \\nIntroduction to Statistics | Types of Statistics | Types of Data | Levels of Measurement \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 2: \\nMeasures of Central Tendency | Measures of Central Tendency in Python | Measures of \\nDispersion | Measures of Dispersion in Python | Random Variables | Sets | Histogram \\nSkewness | Covariance Correlation | Covariance Correlation in Python \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 3: \\nProbability Density Distribution Function | PDF, PMF CDF | ypes of Probability \\nDistribution | Bernoulli Distribution | Binomial Distribution | Poisson Distribution | \\nNormal or Gaussian Distribution \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 4:  \\nUniform Distribution | Z Stats Z Table | Central Limit Theorem \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 5:  \\nEstimate | Hypothesis Testing Mechanism | P value | Z Test with Examples | Student T \\nDistribution | T Stats T Test | When to use T test vs Z test \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 6: \\nType 1 Type 2 Error | Confidence Interval Margin of Error | Bayes Theorem \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 7: \\nWhat is Chi Square Test | Chi Square for Goodness of Fit | Chi Square Test with Python \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 8: \\nF Distribution | Variance Ratio Test ( F test ) | F test with Python \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 9: \\nAnova | Assumptions in Anova | Types of Anova | Partition of variance in Anova'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 279}, page_content='MODULE 7 – Feature Engineering \\n-\\nUNIT 1: \\nAI vs ML vs DL vs DS | Supervised, Unsupervised Reinforcement Learning | Train, Test \\nValidation | Variance, Bias, Overfitting Underfitting \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 2: \\nHandling Missing Values | Handling Imbalanced Dataset | SMOTE | Data Interpolation \\n| Handling Outliers \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 3: \\nFeature Extraction | Feature Scaling Normalization | Normalization Min Max Scaling | \\nUnit Vectors Feature Scaling | PCA   \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 4:  \\nData Encoding | Nominal or One Hot Encoding \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 5:  \\nLabel Ordinal Encoder | Target Guided Ordinal Encoding \\nMODULE 8 – ML: Supervised Machine Learning \\nPART 1 – REGRESSION \\n-\\nUNIT 1: \\n Simple Linear Regression | Multiple Linear Regression | Polynomial Linear Regression \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 2: \\n R squared Adjusted R squared | MSE, MAE RMSE | Simple Linear Regression with \\nPython | Multiple Linear Regression \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 3: \\nRidge Regression | Lasso Regression \\n \\n-\\nUNIT 4:  \\n Elastic Net Regression | EDA With Algerian Forest Fire | Model Training for Ridge, \\nLasso Elastic Net \\nEND TO END ML PROJECT \\n- Weather Prediction: \\nScraping Google Images, involves extracting data from website the project involved \\nsending requests to the Google Images website, parsing the HTML content, and \\nextracting relevant image URLs using BeautifulSoup. This project showcases technical \\nskills in Python programming and data analytics.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 280}, page_content='PART 3 – DECISION TREE \\n-\\nDecision Tree Classifier Intuition \\n-\\nDecision Tree For Numerical Split \\n-\\nPost Pruning And Prepruning Decision Trees \\n-\\nDecision Tree Classifier Implementation \\n-\\nDecision Tree Post Pruning \\n-\\nDecision Tree Regressor in depth Intuition \\n-\\nDecision Tree Regressor Implementation \\nPART 4 – SUPPORT VECTOR MACHINES \\n-\\nSupport Vector Classifier Indepth Intuition \\n-\\nSupport Vector Machines Classifier \\n-\\nSupport Vector Regressor Indepth Intuition \\n-\\nSupport Vector Regressor Implementation \\n-\\nSVM Kernels Intuition \\n-\\nSVM Kernels Implementation \\nEND TO END ML PROJECT \\n- Diabetes Prediction: \\nDiabetes Prediction is a machine learning project for data science designed to forecast \\nthe likelihood of diabetes based on relevant health data. Using predictive modeling, \\nthe project aims to assist in early detection and proactive management of diabetes risk \\nfactors, technical skills in Python programming and data analytics. \\nPART 2 – LOGISTICS REGRESSION \\n-\\nLogistic Regression Indepth Intuition \\n-\\nLogistic Regression with Regularization \\n-\\nPerformance Metrics Confusion Matrix, Accuracy, Precision Recall \\n-\\nCross Validation Types \\n-\\nHyperparameter Tuning \\n-\\nLogistic Regression Implementation \\n-\\nLogistic Regression Multiclass Classification \\nPART 5 – NAIVE BAYES \\n-\\nNaive Bayes Indepth Intuition \\n-\\nVariants Of Naive Bayes Algorithms \\n-\\nNaive Bayes Practical Implementation'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 281}, page_content='PART 6 – ENSEMBLE TECHNIQUES & ITS TYPES \\n-\\nEnsemble Techniques And Bagging \\n-\\nRandom Forest Classifier And Regressor \\n-\\nOut Of Bag Score Decision Trees \\n-\\nRandom Forest Practical Implementation \\nPART 7 – BOOSTING \\n-\\nBoosting Technique \\n-\\nGradient Boosting Indepth Intuition \\n-\\nXgboost Classification Algorithms \\n-\\nXgboost Regressor Algorithm \\nPART 8 – KNN ALGORITHM \\n-\\nKNN Classification And Regression \\n-\\nVariants Of KNN \\n-\\nKNN Classifier and Regr Implementation \\nPART 2 – CLUSTERING ALGORITHMS \\n-\\nK Means Indepth Intuition \\n-\\nHierarichal Clustering Intuition \\n-\\nK means vs Hierarichal Clustering \\n-\\nDBSCAN Clustering \\n-\\nSilhouette Score Clustering \\n-\\nK Means Clustering Implementation \\n-\\nHierarchal Clustering Implementation \\n-\\nDBSCAN Algorithms Implementation \\nEND TO END ML PROJECT \\n- Medical Prediction: \\nMedical Prediction employs machine learning for data science to forecast health \\noutcomes based on relevant medical data. This project aims to enhance predictive \\nanalytics in the medical field for improved diagnosis and patient care technical skills in \\nPython programming and data analytics. \\nMODULE 9 – ML: Unsupervised Machine Learning \\nPART 1 – PCA \\n-\\nCurse Of Dimensionality \\n-\\nGeometric Intuition Behind PCA \\n-\\nMathematical Intuition Of PCA \\n-\\nPCA Practical Implementation'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 282}, page_content='PART 4 – TIME SERIES \\n-\\nIntroduction of time series \\n-\\nComponents of time series \\n-\\nMoving average \\n-\\nStationary and non stationary \\n-\\nAcf pacf \\n-\\nArima \\n-\\nTime sereis model building \\n-\\nTime sereis EDA \\nEND TO END ML PROJECT \\n- Diamond Price Prediction: \\nDiamond Price Prediction is a machine learning project for data science that predicts \\ndiamond prices based on various features. Using algorithms, it aims to provide \\naccurate and data-driven insights for pricing within the diamond industry. \\nMODULE 10 – Neural Network with Deep Learning \\nPART 3 – ANOMALY DETECTION \\n-\\nAnomaly Detection Isolation Fores \\n-\\nDBSCAN Anomaly Detection \\n-\\nLocal Outlier Factor Anamoly Detection \\nPART 1 – NEURAL NETWORK & ITS PERCEPTION \\n-\\nIntro to Deep Learning Usecases \\n-\\nNeural Network, Perceptron Mathematical Explanation \\nPART 2 – NEURAL NETWORK \\n-\\nMathematical Concepts \\n-\\nActivation Functions \\n-\\nForward Back Propagation \\n-\\nImplementation of ANN using Keras \\n-\\nCallback Functions \\nPART 3 – ANN \\n-\\nRegression using ANN \\n-\\nLoss Function \\n-\\nBatch Normalisation \\n-\\nRegularization'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 283}, page_content='PART 5 – CNN \\n-\\n* Convolutional Neural Networks \\n-\\n* CNN Foundation 1 \\n-\\n* CNN 2 \\n-\\n* CNN 3 (Explainer) \\n-\\n* CNN 4 (LENET) \\n-\\n* CNN 5 (Alex Net) \\n-\\n* CNN 6 \\n-\\n* CNN 7 \\n-\\n* VGG NET \\n-\\n* Resnet \\n-\\n* Inception Net \\n-\\n* RCNN \\n-\\n* Fast RCNN \\n-\\n* Faster RCNN (Object Detection) \\n-\\n* Non Maximum Suppression \\nPART 6 – YOLO \\n-\\n* YOLO \\n-\\n* YOLO V2 \\n-\\n* YOLO V3 \\n-\\n* YOLO V4 \\n-\\n* YOLO V4 Part 2 \\n-\\n* YOLO V5 \\nPART 4 – TENSOR FLOW & PYTORCH \\n-\\n Regularisation in Deep Learning \\n-\\n Weight Initialisation \\n-\\n Optimizers \\n-\\n Tensorflow \\n-\\n Pytorch \\nEND TO END ML PROJECT \\n- Credit Card Fault Detection: \\nCredit Card Fault Detection is a deep learning project for data science focused on \\nidentifying fraudulent transactions within credit card data. Leveraging neural \\nnetworks, the project aims to enhance the accuracy of fraud detection algorithms for \\nsecure financial transactions. \\nPART 7 – GAN \\n* GAN Introduction \\n* Training using GAN \\n* DC GAN \\n* Style GAN \\n* W Gan & GAN Practical'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 284}, page_content='\\uf0b7 LEVEL 3 :- AI SUBSET : \\nDeep Learning, NLP  &  Computer Vision \\nMODULE 11 – Deep Learning for AI Engineers \\nFoundations of Neural Networks \\n-\\nIntroduction to the building blocks of deep learning. Covers the transition from \\nlinear regression to the perceptron, activation functions (ReLU, Sigmoid, Tanh), \\nforward propagation, and the mathematics of backpropagation using gradient \\ndescent. Neurons, weights, biases, loss functions, and optimization. \\nConvolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) for Computer Vision \\n-\\nFocused on processing grid-structured data like images. This section covers spatial \\nhierarchy, feature extraction, and how deep learning revolutionizes computer \\nvision tasks. Convolutional layers, pooling, stride, padding, and classic architectures \\n(e.g., ResNet, EfficientNet) for image classification and object detection. \\nDeep Network Training & Optimization \\n-\\nMoving beyond basic training to stabilize and accelerate deep networks.  Students \\nlearn how to combat overfitting, manage vanishing/exploding gradients, and tune \\nhyperparameters \\neffectively. \\nBatch \\nNormalization, \\nDropout, \\nand \\nweight \\ninitialization strategies. \\nRecurrent Neural Networks (RNNs) & Sequence Modeling \\n-\\nAn introduction to handling sequential data where time or order matters, such as \\ntext, time-series, or audio. Vanilla RNNs, Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) \\nnetworks, Gated Recurrent Units (GRUs), and the limitations of sequential \\nprocessing. \\nThe Transformer Architecture & Attention Mechanisms \\n-\\nWhy attention mechanisms replaced RNNs, allowing for massive parallelization and \\nthe rise of Large Language Models (LLMs). Self-attention, multi-head attention, \\npositional encoding, Encoder-Decoder architecture, and BERT/GPT foundations.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 285}, page_content='Generative AI & Deep Generative Models \\n-\\nExploration of models that create new data instances. This bridges traditional deep learning \\nwith modern generative engineering. Variational Autoencoders (VAEs), Generative \\nAdversarial Networks (GANs), and Diffusion Models (the tech behind image generators like \\nStable Diffusion). \\nMLOps: Deep Learning Deployment & Scaling \\n-\\nEssential for AI Engineers (as opposed to research scientists). This section focuses on taking \\na trained deep learning model and serving it efficiently to users. Model quantization and \\npruning, GPU/TPU acceleration, containerization (Docker), and deployment via APIs \\n(FastAPI, Triton Inference Server). \\nMODULE 12 – NLP : Natural Language Processing  \\nPART 1 \\n-\\nIntroduction to NLP \\n-\\nHistory of NLP \\n-\\nWhy NLP \\n-\\nUse of NLP \\n-\\nweb scrapping \\n-\\nText processing \\n-\\nUnderstanding regex \\nPART 2 \\n-\\n* String Tokenization \\n-\\n* Sentence Processing \\n-\\n* Word Embedding \\n-\\n* Lemmatization in text processing \\n-\\n* Frequency Distribution \\n-\\n* Annotator creation \\n-\\n* Word Count \\n-\\n* Text Normalization \\n-\\n* Word 2 Vec \\n-\\n* Co Occurance Vector \\nPART 3 - NLP \\n-\\n* Doc 2 Vec \\n-\\n* Text blob \\n-\\n* NLTK \\n-\\n* Gensim \\n-\\n* RNN \\n-\\n* LSTM \\n-\\n* BI LSTM'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 286}, page_content='NLP PROJECT \\n- Smart Voice Response System: \\nSpeech-to-Speech Project, this project focuses on developing a system that takes \\nspoken input and generates spoken output in another form, such as language \\ntranslation or conversational responses. It highlights how speech technologies can be \\napplied in communication tools, translation systems, and interactive assistants. \\nNLP PROJECT \\n- Voice-to-Text Converter: \\nSpeech-to-Text Project, this project focuses on building a system that converts spoken \\nlanguage into written text. It is commonly used in transcription services, voice-\\ncommand applications, and digital assistants, making it an essential component in \\nmodern speech and language technologies. \\nMODULE 13 – Computer Vision  (Open CV) \\n- Computer Vision in data science focuses on enabling machines to interpret \\nand make decisions based on visual data. It involves developing algorithms \\nand models to analyze images or videos, extracting meaningful information \\nfor applications like image segmentation, object detection, and scene \\nrecognition. \\n- Detection of Objects detection in computer vision is the process of \\nidentifying and locating specific objects within images or videos. Using \\nadvanced algorithms, this technology enables machines to recognize and \\ndraw bounding boxes around objects. \\n-\\nScene Recognition in computer vision involves teaching machines to \\nunderstand and categorize the overall context or setting within an image. \\nThrough sophisticated algorithms, this technology enables systems to \\nidentify and classify scenes. \\n-\\nImage Segmentation in computer vision is the process of dividing an image \\ninto meaningful segments or regions. This technique, facilitated by \\nadvanced algorithms, allows for precise identification and extraction of \\nobjects within an image.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 287}, page_content='Unit 1: Introduction \\n\\uf0b7\\nConcept of AI in automation  \\n\\uf0b7\\nWorkflows, Agents, and Pipelines (basic idea)  \\nUnit 2: Communication Automation \\n\\uf0b7\\nEmail drafting and replies  \\n\\uf0b7\\nBasic message handling and organization  \\nUnit 3: Meeting & Text Processing \\n\\uf0b7\\nTranscription of meetings  \\n\\uf0b7\\nExtracting key points and actions  \\nUnit 4: Document Handling \\n\\uf0b7\\nProcessing documents and forms  \\n\\uf0b7\\nExtracting useful information  \\nCOMPUTER VISION PROJECT 1  \\n- Object Tracking: \\nObject Tracking in computer vision for data science involves developing algorithms to \\nfollow and analyze the movement of objects. This project aims to enhance real-time \\ntracking capabilities for applications such as surveillance and autonomous systems. \\nCOMPUTER VISION PROJECT 2 \\n- Image Classification: \\nImage Classification in computer vision for data science focuses on developing \\nalgorithms to categorize and label images based on their content. This project aims to \\nimprove automated image recognition systems for various applications. \\nCOMPUTER VISION PROJECT 3 \\n- Image to Text: \\nImage to Text in computer vision for data science involves converting visual content \\ninto text using machine learning algorithms. This project aims to enhance accessibility \\nand information retrieval by enabling automated extraction of textual information \\nfrom images. \\nMODULE 14 – AI Workflow Automation'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 288}, page_content='Unit 5: Monitoring & Analysis \\n\\uf0b7\\nTracking data (e.g., revenue, feedback)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nBasic sentiment analysis  \\nUnit 6: Data Integration \\n\\uf0b7\\nUsing AI with sheets and simple tools  \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntroduction to APIs and NLP  \\nUnit 7: Multi Media Automation \\n\\uf0b7\\nScheduling and managing posts  \\n\\uf0b7\\nAvoiding common errors \\nMODULE 15 – Multi Agent System \\nUnit 1: Introduction to Agents \\n\\uf0b7\\nFoundations: chatbots, assistants, and voice agents  \\n\\uf0b7\\nConcept of single-agent vs multi-agent systems  \\nUnit 2: Knowledge & Retrieval \\n\\uf0b7\\nBasics of knowledge bases  \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntroduction to Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)  \\nUnit 3: Bot Development \\n\\uf0b7\\nBuilding no-code bots  \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntegration with platforms (e.g., messaging apps like WhatsApp)  \\nUnit 4: Conversational Design \\n\\uf0b7\\nDefining persona, tone, and brand voice  \\n\\uf0b7\\nDesigning effective conversational flows  \\nUnit 5: Context & Query Handling \\n\\uf0b7\\nUnderstanding user queries  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMaintaining context in conversations'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 289}, page_content='TRANSFORMER PROJECT \\n Text Transformation Project \\nIn this project, you will build a model that transforms one piece of text into \\nanother, such as summarization or translation. It highlights the core power \\nof Natural Language Processing (NLP) and strengthens your practical \\nunderstanding of text processing. This project strengthens your practical \\nunderstanding of Natural Language Processing (NLP) and helps you gain \\nhands-on experience in text transformation tasks. \\nTransformers  \\n* What are Transformers \\n* Self-Attention Basics \\n* Encoder and Decoder Blocks \\n* Applications in NLP and Vision \\n\\uf0b7 LEVEL 4 :- AI ENGINEERING \\nAdvance GEN AI Ecosystem \\nMODULE 16 – Transformer \\nTransformers & Large Language Models \\n* Introduction to Transformers \\n* Self-Attention Mechanism \\n* Encoder-Decoder Structure \\n* Positional Encoding \\n* Role in Large Language Models (LLMs) \\nRecurrent Neural Network  \\n* Sequential Data Handling \\n* Hidden State Concept \\n* Limitations of RNNs (vanishing gradient) \\nMODULE 17 – RNN (Recurrent Neural Network)'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 290}, page_content='UNIT - 2 Hidden State Concept   \\n \\n2.1 Definition: Hidden state as internal memory of RNN  \\n2.2 Mathematical Representation \\n2.3 Components \\n \\n2.4 Properties of Hidden State  \\n \\n2.5 Role in Learning \\nUNIT - 1 Sequential Data Handling  \\n \\n1.1 Introduction \\n\\uf0b7\\nDefinition of sequential data  \\n\\uf0b7\\nImportance of order in data processing  \\n1.2 Characteristics of Sequential Data \\n\\uf0b7\\nTemporal dependency  \\n\\uf0b7\\nContextual relationships  \\n\\uf0b7\\nNon-independence of data points  \\n1.3 Types of Sequential Data \\n\\uf0b7\\nText data (NLP)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nTime-series data  \\n\\uf0b7\\nAudio and speech data  \\n1.4 Sequential Processing in RNNs \\n\\uf0b7\\nStep-by-step input processing  \\n\\uf0b7\\nTime steps and sequence flow  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMaintaining continuity across inputs  \\n1.5 Applications \\n\\uf0b7\\nLanguage modeling  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMachine translation  \\n\\uf0b7\\nSentiment analysis  \\n\\uf0b7\\nForecasting systems'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 291}, page_content='Unit 1: Introduction to LSTM \\n\\uf0b7\\nDefinition of  LSTM (advanced RNN architecture)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nNeed for LSTM over traditional RNNs  \\n\\uf0b7\\nHandling long-term dependencies \\nUnit 3: Limitations of RNNs (Vanishing Gradient Problem)  \\n \\n3.1 Introduction \\nOverview of training challenges in RNNs \\n \\n3.2 Vanishing Gradient Problem \\nDefinition and explanation \\nOccurrence in backpropagation through time (BPTT) \\n \\n3.3 Causes \\nRepeated multiplication of small gradient values \\nExponential decay over long sequences \\n \\n3.4 Effects \\nLoss of long-term dependencies \\nSlow or no learning in early layers \\nBias toward recent inputs \\n \\n3.5 Related Issue \\nExploding gradient problem \\n \\nLSTM — Long Short Term Memory \\n \\n* Cell State and Gates \\n* Forget Gate, Input Gate, Output Gate \\n* Solving Vanishing Gradient Problem \\n* Applications in Text & Speech \\nMODULE 18 – LSTM — Long Short Term Memory'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 292}, page_content='Unit 2: Cell State and Gates \\n\\uf0b7\\nConcept of cell state (long-term memory)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRole of gates in controlling information flow  \\n\\uf0b7\\nTypes of gates: Forget, Input, Output  \\nUnit 3: LSTM Gates Mechanism \\n3.1 Forget Gate \\n\\uf0b7\\nDecides what information to discard  \\n\\uf0b7\\nUses sigmoid function to filter data  \\n3.2 Input Gate \\n\\uf0b7\\nDecides what new information to store  \\n\\uf0b7\\nUpdates the cell state  \\n3.3 Output Gate \\n\\uf0b7\\nControls what information is passed as output  \\n\\uf0b7\\nDetermines next hidden state \\nUnit 4: Solving Vanishing Gradient Problem \\n\\uf0b7\\nLSTM maintains constant error flow via cell state  \\n\\uf0b7\\nReduces gradient decay over long sequences  \\n\\uf0b7\\nEnables learning of long-term dependencies  \\nUnit 5: Applications in Text & Speech \\n\\uf0b7\\nText generation and language modelling  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMachine translation  \\n\\uf0b7\\nSpeech recognition  \\n\\uf0b7\\nSentiment analysis \\n \\nForward & Backpropagation \\n \\n* Forward Pass Basics \\n* Loss Function Calculation \\n* Backpropagation and Weight Updates \\nMODULE 19 – Generative  AI — Forward & Back Propagation'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 293}, page_content='Unit 1: Introduction \\n\\uf0b7\\nBasics of neural networks  \\n\\uf0b7\\nOverview of training process  \\nUnit 2: Forward Pass \\n\\uf0b7\\nConcept of forward pass  \\n\\uf0b7\\nInput to output flow in a network  \\n\\uf0b7\\nActivation functions (basic idea)  \\nUnit 3: Loss Function \\n\\uf0b7\\nPurpose of loss function  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCalculating error between predicted and actual output  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCommon loss functions (overview)  \\nUnit 4: Backpropagation \\n\\uf0b7\\nConcept of backpropagation  \\n\\uf0b7\\nError propagation through layers  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRole of gradients  \\nUnit 5: Weight Updates \\n\\uf0b7\\nUpdating weights using gradients  \\n\\uf0b7\\nLearning rate concept  \\n\\uf0b7\\nBasic optimization process  \\nMODULE 20 – (CNNs , Tensor Flow & Pytorch) \\nCNN — Convolutional Neural Network \\n \\n* Convolution Layer \\n* Pooling Layer \\n* Fully Connected Layer \\n* Applications in Image Processing'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 294}, page_content='Tensor Flow \\n \\n* Introduction and Features \\n* Tensors Basics \\n* Building Neural Networks in TensorFlow \\n* Applications in AI & ML \\n \\nPyTorch \\n \\n* Introduction and Features \\n* Tensors in PyTorch \\n* Autograd Functionality \\n* Model Training with PyTorch \\n \\nHugging Face \\n \\n* Introduction to Hugging Face \\n* Transformers Library \\n* Pre-trained Models (BERT, GPT, etc.) \\n* Applications in NLP \\nProject 1 — Telegram Chatbot with LLM Integration \\n \\nThis project focuses on converting written text into natural-sounding \\nspeech. It demonstrates the process of transforming text into voice and \\nhelps you gain hands-on experience in speech generation. It provides \\nhands-on experience in creating voice-enabled systems and understanding \\nthe underlying concepts of text-to-speech technology. \\n Project 2 — Text-to-Speech Conversion Project \\n \\nThis project focuses on converting written text into natural-sounding \\nspeech. It demonstrates the process of transforming text into voice and \\nhelps you gain hands-on experience in speech generation. It provides \\nhands-on experience in creating voice-enabled systems and understanding \\nthe underlying concepts of text-to-speech technology.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 295}, page_content='LEVEL 5  \\nAI Engineering Advance Agentic Modules \\nMODULE 21 – Agentic AI & Types of Agent \\n Agentic AI Introduction \\n \\n-\\n What is Agentic AI and how it differs from traditional AI systems \\n-\\n Key characteristics: autonomy, adaptability, and intelligent decision- \\n  making \\n-\\n  Real-world examples of Agentic AI \\n-\\n  Benefits of Agentic AI in solving dynamic and complex problems \\n-\\n  Challenges and limitations in practical applications \\n-\\nAgentic AI Lifecycle \\n \\n-\\nStages of an AI agent \\n-\\nContinuous learning and improvement in live environments \\n-\\nImportance of performance evaluation and feedback loops \\n-\\nBest practices for maintaining robust and scalable agentic systems \\n-\\nTypes of Agents \\n \\n-\\nSimple Reflex \\n-\\nModel-Based Agents \\n-\\nGoal-Based Agents \\n-\\nUtility-Based Agents \\n-\\nComparison of agent types \\n-\\nSingle vs. Multi-Agent Models \\n \\n-\\nDefinition and characteristics of single-agent systems \\n-\\nOverview of multi-agent systems (MAS) \\n-\\nInteraction patterns: cooperation, competition, and coordination \\n-\\nUse cases of MAS in real-world applications \\n-\\nChallenges in communication, conflict resolution, and scalability'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 296}, page_content='MODULE 22 – Decision Making Mechanism RL & LLMs \\nFoundations of Agentic Decision-Making \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntroduction to Agentic AI and Autonomous Systems  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCharacteristics of Intelligent Agents (Reactive vs Deliberative vs Hybrid)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nAgent Architecture Overview (Perception–Reasoning–Action loop)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nTypes of Environments (Fully/Partially Observable, Deterministic, \\nStochastic)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRationality and Utility-Based Decision Making \\nPerception – Understanding the Environment \\n\\uf0b7\\nRole of Sensors and Data Inputs in AI Agents  \\n\\uf0b7\\nStructured vs Unstructured Data Processing  \\n\\uf0b7\\nState Representation and World Modeling  \\n\\uf0b7\\nFeature Extraction and Context Awareness  \\n\\uf0b7\\nHandling Noisy and Incomplete Data  \\n\\uf0b7\\nReal-world Examples: Chatbots, Robotics, Recommendation Systems \\nAction Selection & Execution \\n\\uf0b7\\nMapping Decisions to Actions  \\n\\uf0b7\\nAction Policies and Policy Optimization  \\n\\uf0b7\\nReal-time Decision Execution  \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntegration with APIs, Tools, and External Systems  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMulti-step Task Execution in Agentic Workflows  \\n\\uf0b7\\nSafety, Constraints, and Ethical Boundaries in Actions \\nHandling Uncertainty & Dynamic Environments \\n\\uf0b7\\nSources of Uncertainty in Real-world Systems  \\n\\uf0b7\\nProbabilistic Reasoning (Bayesian Inference)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nAdaptive Decision-Making Strategies  \\n\\uf0b7\\nExploration vs Exploitation Trade-off  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRobustness in Changing Environments  \\n\\uf0b7\\nScenario-based Decision Simulation'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 297}, page_content='MODULE 23 – Lang Chain & Lang Graph & OLLAMA \\nIntroduction to Lang Chain \\n\\uf0b7\\nOverview of Lang Chain for building agentic applications  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRole of LLM frameworks in AI system design  \\n\\uf0b7\\nUse cases: chatbots, automation agents, RAG systems \\nCore Components of Lang Chain \\n\\uf0b7\\nChains: Sequential and conditional workflows  \\n\\uf0b7\\nAgents: Tool-using intelligent systems  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMemory: Short-term and long-term context handling  \\n\\uf0b7\\nPrompts and output parsers \\nIntegrating LLMs with Tools \\n\\uf0b7\\nConnecting APIs, databases, and external services  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) basics  \\n\\uf0b7\\nTool calling and function execution  \\n\\uf0b7\\nWorkflow orchestration with Lang Chain \\nLang Graph for Advanced Workflows \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntroduction to Lang Graph and stateful agents  \\n\\uf0b7\\nGraph-based workflow design  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMulti-step reasoning and branching logic  \\n\\uf0b7\\nBuilding multi-agent systems \\nHands-on with Lang Chain \\n\\uf0b7\\nBuilding a simple chatbot  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCreating an agent with tool usage  \\n\\uf0b7\\nImplementing memory in applications  \\n\\uf0b7\\nDesigning end-to-end AI workflows'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 298}, page_content='Production Benefits of Lang Chain \\n\\uf0b7\\nScalability and modular architecture  \\n\\uf0b7\\nFaster development and prototyping  \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntegration flexibility  \\n\\uf0b7\\nMonitoring, debugging, and optimization  \\nIntroduction to OLLAMA \\n\\uf0b7\\nRunning LLMs locally using Ollama  \\n\\uf0b7\\nSetup and basic commands  \\n\\uf0b7\\nLocal vs cloud-based LLMs  \\nRAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Models \\n\\uf0b7\\nArchitecture of RAG: Retrieval system + Generative model  \\n\\uf0b7\\nHow RAG retrieves relevant data and generates coherent responses  \\n\\uf0b7\\nComparison with traditional LLM-only approaches  \\n\\uf0b7\\nAdvantages: accuracy, context-awareness, reduced hallucination  \\n\\uf0b7\\nUse cases: enterprise AI, research, knowledge management systems \\nFeatures & Benefits \\n\\uf0b7\\nPrivacy and data security  \\n\\uf0b7\\nOffline access and low latency  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCustomization and control over models  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCost efficiency \\nModels & Deployment \\n\\uf0b7\\nSupported models (LLaMA, Mistral, etc.)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nModel selection strategies  \\n\\uf0b7\\nDeployment options (local machine, server setup) \\nMODULE 24 – RAG, DataStax & Lang Flow'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 299}, page_content='RAG in Agentic AI Workflows \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntegrating RAG with agent-based systems  \\n\\uf0b7\\nContext-aware decision-making using external knowledge  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCombining tools, memory, and retrieval in workflows  \\n\\uf0b7\\nDesigning intelligent knowledge-driven agents \\nIntroduction to DataStax \\n\\uf0b7\\nOverview of DataStax as a scalable vector database solution  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRole of vector databases in modern AI systems  \\n\\uf0b7\\nStoring embeddings and semantic search basics \\nDataStax in RAG Pipelines \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntegration with LLMs and RAG architectures  \\n\\uf0b7\\nEfficient data storage and retrieval for AI applications  \\n\\uf0b7\\nQuerying large-scale AI datasets  \\n\\uf0b7\\nEnterprise-grade scalability and reliability \\nBest Practices with DataStax \\n\\uf0b7\\nDatabase design for AI workloads  \\n\\uf0b7\\nIndexing and performance optimization  \\n\\uf0b7\\nHandling large-scale data efficiently  \\n\\uf0b7\\nSecurity and enterprise deployment considerations \\nLangflow Framework \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntroduction to Langflow (visual AI workflow builder)  \\n\\uf0b7\\nDrag-and-drop interface for designing pipelines  \\n\\uf0b7\\nRapid prototyping without heavy coding \\nBuilding Workflows with Langflow \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntegrating LLMs, APIs, and data sources  \\n\\uf0b7\\nCreating RAG-based pipelines visually  \\n\\uf0b7\\nConnecting tools, memory, and agents  \\n\\uf0b7\\nTesting and iterating workflows'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 300}, page_content='Projects - AI Agents  \\nPROJECT 01 \\nRAG AI Agent (Retrieval-Augmented Generation Agent) \\nLearn how to build an AI agent that combines information retrieval with text \\ngeneration. This project will show how AI can fetch relevant data from documents or \\nknowledge bases and generate accurate, contextual responses — just like modern AI \\nchatbots. \\nMODULE 25 – Bots & Agents \\nIntroduction to Bots & Agents \\n\\uf0b7\\nOverview of AI bots and intelligent agents  \\n\\uf0b7\\nTypes: rule-based bots, AI agents, autonomous agents  \\n\\uf0b7\\nReal-world applications: chatbots, assistants, automation systems \\nFundamentals of Agent Design \\n\\uf0b7\\nComponents: perception, reasoning, action  \\n\\uf0b7\\nIntegrating LLMs, tools, and memory  \\n\\uf0b7\\nBasics of agent workflows and architectures \\nDeployment & Optimization \\n\\uf0b7\\nTesting and debugging AI agents  \\n\\uf0b7\\nPerformance improvement and scalability  \\n\\uf0b7\\nBasic deployment options (local/cloud) \\nPROJECT 02 \\n   Plant Disease Detection AI Agent \\nWork on a real-world computer vision project where AI identifies plant diseases from \\nleaf images. This project is highly practical in agriculture, showing how AI can support \\nfarmers with early disease detection and better crop management.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 301}, page_content=\"ADDITIONAL MODULE S \\nCrafting an Impressive Resume \\nCrafting an ATS-Friendly Resume - A resume is a summary of your career, \\nskills, and achievements. In this program, you'll also learn how to create a \\nresume that is ATS (Applicant Tracking System) friendly. An ATS is the \\nsoftware most companies use to filter and organize resumes, so making your \\nresume ATS-friendly ensures it is easily readable by these systems as well as \\nby recruiters. \\nPROJECT 03 \\n   Personal AI Assistant Agent \\nBuild your own AI-powered virtual assistant that can answer queries, manage tasks, \\nand interact naturally with users. This project demonstrates how AI can enhance \\nproductivity and provide personalized support in daily life. \\nMock Interview & Tips \\nInterview tips will help you gain valuable insights into effective \\ncommunication and key strategies to showcase your skills confidently. \\nOnline face-to-face mock interviews help you train & prepare for job \\ninterviews in a no-pressure, stress-free environment simulating a real job \\ninterview. Mock interviews will be conducted for you in this course. \\nPortfolio Building \\nA portfolio helps you to organize information so that you're always ready to \\napply for jobs. Your portfolio creates an image of you in an employer's mind. \\nIn this curriculum, you will learn about building the best portfolio. \\nAI Mock Interview \\nAI Mock Interviews use real-time conversational AI to simulate job interviews. \\nYou receive instant, personalized feedback on your answers, communication \\nstyle, and body language. Features include tailorable role-specific scenarios, \\ninteractive follow-up questions, resume-based tailoring, and data-driven \\nperformance analytics to refine your delivery, build confidence, and help you \\nace the actual interview.\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 302}, page_content='20+ AI Tools \\n## Introduction to Prompt Engineering \\nIntroduction to Prompt Engineering covers the fundamentals of designing \\neffective prompts to interact with AI models. It includes structuring \\nquestions, providing context, and experimenting with different prompt \\ntechniques to generate accurate and relevant AI outputs. \\n## ChatGPT \\nA versatile AI assistant by OpenAI that excels in answering questions, \\nwriting content, coding, and problem-solving. It is widely used for learning, \\nautomation, and boosting productivity. \\n## Gemini \\nGoogle’s powerful multimodal AI model that can understand text, images, \\nand code. It is best for research, reasoning, and creating advanced AI-driven \\napplications. \\n## NotebookLM \\nAn AI research assistant that summarizes, organizes, and explains \\ndocuments. It is highly useful for students, researchers, and professionals to \\nstudy and work efficiently. \\n## Grok \\nKnown for its lightning-fast AI processing speed, making responses almost \\nreal-time. It is mainly used for chatbot’s, analytics, and high-performance AI \\ntasks. \\n## Perplexity \\nAn AI-powered search engine that delivers accurate answers with cited \\nsources. It is ideal for research, fact-checking, and exploring topics in depth. \\n## Claude \\nAnthropic’s AI assistant designed with safety and reasoning at its core. It is \\nused for thoughtful writing, coding help, and intelligent conversations.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 303}, page_content='## Gamma AI \\nA tool that creates professional presentations, documents, and webpages \\nquickly. It is best for professionals and students who need high-quality \\ndesigns effortlessly. \\n## MidJourney \\nAn AI image generator that creates stunning and artistic visuals from text \\nprompts. It is widely used by designers, marketers, and creative \\nprofessionals. \\n## Leonardo AI \\nA creative design tool for generating game assets, digital art, and graphics. \\nIt is ideal for artists and content creators looking for customizable visuals. \\n## Freepik \\nA platform offering AI-generated stock photos, vectors, and illustrations. It \\nis useful for marketers, designers, and businesses that need ready-to-use \\nvisuals. \\n## Krea AI \\nA creative AI tool that generates unique images, animations, and concept \\nart. It is best for storytellers, designers, and digital creators. \\n## OpenAI Sora \\nA groundbreaking AI that transforms text into realistic, high-quality videos. \\nIt is perfect for filmmakers, advertisers, and storytellers. \\n## Google AI Studio \\nA developer platform to test, explore, and deploy Google’s AI models. It is \\nmainly used for building, scaling, and integrating AI applications. \\n## Notion AI \\nEnhances the Notion workspace by helping with writing, summarizing, and \\nbrainstorming. It is highly useful for productivity, project management, and \\nnote-taking.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 304}, page_content='THANK YOU \\nMore Details Contact \\nCall or WhatsApp: +91- 7880-113-112  \\nEmail: contact@theiscale.com \\nWebsite:  www.theiscale.com'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 305}, page_content='Statistics Full Course \\nNotes  \\n \\n Contact  - 78801-13112 \\n                        www.theiscale.com'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 306}, page_content='Statistics \\nWebsite –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\n•\\nWhat is Statistics\\n•\\nTypes of statistics\\n•\\nDescriptive statistics\\n•\\nInferential Statistics\\n•\\nMeasure of central tendency\\n•\\nMean, mode, median\\n•\\nPopulation mean, Sample mean\\n•\\nFinding mean – manual calculation \\n•\\nMean using numpy\\n•\\nMean using stats\\n•\\nAverage of the data set\\n•\\nMedian\\n•\\nWhy Median is different from mean\\n•\\nMedian using numpy\\n•\\nMedian using Statistics\\n•\\nMedian using Pandas\\n• Evaluating median in a dataset\\n• Mode\\n• Scipy Library\\n• Mode using statistics module\\n• Uisng Scipy library\\n• Handling multimodal datasets\\n• Measure of  Dispersion\\n• Range\\n• Variance\\n• Population & sample variance\\n• Why sample variance formula is different than \\npopulation\\n• Variance using Numpy\\n• Variance using Pandas\\n• Variance using Scipy\\n• Standard Deviation\\n• Standard Deviation using numpy'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 307}, page_content='Statistics \\nWebsite –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\n•\\nStandard Deviation using \\npandas\\n•\\nDeviation using Scipy\\n•\\nData Distribution\\n•\\nNormal/Gaussian Disribution\\n•\\nGaussian distribution - code\\n•\\nSkewness\\n•\\nRight skewed curve\\n•\\nPositive skew curve - code\\n•\\nLeft skewed curve\\n•\\nNegative skew curve - code\\n•\\nUniform Distribution \\n•\\nCode for uniform distribution\\n•\\nBi-modal distribution\\n•\\nCode for Bi-modal curve\\n•\\nMultimodal distribution\\n•\\nCode for Histogram multimodal\\n• Inferential statistics\\n• Estimate\\n• Point estimate\\n• Interval estimate\\n• Confidence interval\\n• Significance value\\n• Hypothesis testing\\n• Mechanism for hypothesis testing\\n• P-test\\n• P- test use case via code\\n• T –test\\n• T-test use case via code\\n• Z – test\\n• Z- table\\n• Z- test use case via code\\n• Two test trail\\n• Practice questions'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 308}, page_content='Statistics \\nWebsite –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nFor which Job Roles can this statistics course be helpful?\\n•\\nData Scientist\\n•\\nData Analyst\\n•\\nBusiness Analyst \\n•\\nMachine Learning Engineers\\n•\\nAI Engineers\\n•\\nBI Developers'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 309}, page_content='Statistics \\nWebsite –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nWhy are we studying statistics for data science?'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 310}, page_content='Statistics \\nWebsite –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nData Science & Analytics\\nWhy are we studying statistics for data science?'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 311}, page_content='Statistics \\nWebsite –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nWhy are we studying statistics for data science?\\nDescriptive Statistics \\nRegression Analysis\\nk-means clustering\\nA/B testing \\ntime series analysis'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 312}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nTypes of Statistics\\nDescriptive Statistics\\nInferential Statistics\\nDescriptive statistics ka kaam hai kisi bhi \\ndataset ke main features ko summarize, \\nanalyze, visualize aur describe karna.\\nInferential statistics ka use karke hum ek chhoti si \\nsample data se puri population ke baare mein \\npredictions ya inferences bana sakte hain.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 313}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nDescriptive Statistics\\nDescriptive statistics ka kaam hai kisi bhi \\ndataset ke main features ko summarize, \\nanalyze, visualize aur describe karna.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 314}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nDescriptive Statistics\\nDescriptive statistics ka kaam hai kisi bhi dataset ke main features ko summarize, analyze, visualize aur \\ndescribe karna. Iska main purpose yeh hota hai ki hum data ke andar chhipe hue patterns ko samajh sakein \\naur unhe simple terms mein explain kar sakein. \\nCommon Techniques\\nMeasures of Central Tendency - Mean (average), Median, aur Mode\\nMeasures of Variability - Range, Variance, Standard Deviation\\nData Representation - Charts, graphs, tables,  frequency distributions'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 315}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nInferential Statistics (Inferential Statistics) ka purpose hota hai kisi sample data ka use karke \\npopulation ke baare mein conclusions aur predictions banana. Yeh statistics ke ek branch \\nhai jo data analysis ke baad generalized statements aur hypotheses test karne mein madad \\nkarta hai.\\nCommon Techniques\\nHypothesis Testing\\nConfidence Intervals\\nRegression Analysis\\n Correlation'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 316}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question 1\\nWhat is Descriptive Statistics?\\nA. A method to predict future trends\\nB. A method to summarize and organize data\\nC. A method to test hypotheses\\nD. A method to establish a relationship between two variables'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 317}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question 2\\nWhich of the following techniques is used in Inferential Statistics?\\nA. Mean\\nB. Hypothesis Testing\\nC. Frequency Distribution\\nD. Median'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 318}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question 3\\nWhat is the main difference between Descriptive and Inferential Statistics?\\nA. Descriptive statistics summarize data, while inferential statistics make predictions \\nor inferences about a population\\nB. Descriptive statistics are based on probability, while inferential statistics are not\\nC. Inferential statistics focus on organizing data, while descriptive statistics focus on \\nmaking predictions\\nD. Both deal with making predictions about data'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 319}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nMeasure of Central Tendency\\nMeasures of Central ka matlab hota hai data set ke center ko samajhna. Inka use karke hum jaan sakte \\nhain ki data ke values kis jagah ke aas-paas clustered hain. Yeh three main types ke hote hain: Mean, \\nMedian, aur Mode.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 320}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nMean\\nMean ek statistical measure hai jo central tendency ko represent karta hai. Yeh ek dataset ke sabhi \\nvalues ka average hota hai. Hum mean ko do tarikon se calculate karte hain: Population Mean aur \\nSample Mean.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 321}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPopulation Mean\\nPopulation Mean tab calculate kiya jata hai jab aapke paas poore population ka data available ho. Population mean ko \\nµ se denote kiya jata hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 322}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nSample Mean\\nSample Mean tab calculate kiya jata hai jab aap population se ek chhota sample lete hain. Sample mean \\nko x̄ se denote kiya jata hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 323}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nMedian\\nThe median is a measure of central tendency that represents the middle value of a dataset when it is \\narranged in ascending or descending order. Unlike the mean, the median is not affected by outliers or \\nskewed data, making it a more robust measure for datasets with extreme values.\\nSteps to Calculate the Median\\n1.Sort the dataset in ascending or descending order.\\n2.Determine the number of observations n.\\n3.Apply the appropriate formula depending on whether n is odd or even.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 324}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nMode\\nIn statistics, the mode is a measure of central tendency that represents the value that appears most \\nfrequently in a dataset. Unlike the mean (average) and median (middle value), the mode focuses solely \\non the frequency of values.\\nConsider the following dataset of exam scores:\\n[85, 90, 90, 95, 85, 80, 85, 90, 80]\\nList Frequencies:\\n85 appears 3 times\\n90 appears 4 times\\n95 appears 1 time\\n80 appears 2 times\\nDetermine Mode:\\nThe value 90 appears most frequently (4 times), so 90 is the mode of this dataset.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 325}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nScipy Library\\nThe scipy library is a powerful open-source Python library used for scientific and technical \\ncomputing. It builds on the numpy library and provides a wide range of functionalities for \\ndifferent types of scientific and engineering tasks. \\nThe scipy library is widely used in various fields, including:\\n•\\nEngineering: For optimizing designs and control systems.\\n•\\nFinance: To optimize investment portfolios and forecast economic trends.\\n•\\nMedical Imaging: Enhances and analyzes diagnostic images.\\n•\\nData Science: Fills missing data and optimizes machine learning models.\\n•\\nSignal Processing: Analyzes audio and vibration signals for better quality and maintenance.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 326}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question 1\\nIf the mode of a data set is 10, what does this imply?\\na) 10 is the most frequently occurring value in the data set\\nb) 10 is the average of the data set\\nc) 10 is the middle value when the data is sorted\\nd) 10 is the sum of all values divided by the number of values'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 327}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question 2\\nIf a data set is perfectly symmetrical, which of the following statements is \\ntrue?\\na) The mean is less than the median\\nb) The mean is greater than the median\\nc) The mean and median are equal\\nd) The mode and median are always equal'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 328}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question 3\\nIn which situation is the mean not a good measure of central tendency?\\na) When the data set has extreme outliers\\nb) When the data set is normally distributed\\nc) When the data set has a small number of values\\nd) When the data set is uniformly distributed'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 329}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nMeasure of Dispersion\\nMeasure of dispersion , statistics mein data ke spread ya spread out hone ki extent ko measure karta hai. Ye \\nbataata hai ki data points ek mean value se kitne door hain. Inka use data ke distribution ko samajhne aur \\ncompare karne ke liye hota hai.\\nAgar hum sirf mean (average) dekhte hain, to humein yeh nahi pata chalta ki data points mean se kitna door hain. \\nIsliye dispersion ki measures help karti hain humein yeh samajhne mein ki data kitna spread out hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 330}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nMeasure of Dispersion\\nRange\\nVariance\\nStandard Deviation'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 331}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nRange\\nIn descriptive statistics, range is a simple measure of variability or spread in a data set. It \\nindicates how far the data points are spread out by showing the difference between the \\nmaximum and minimum values in the dataset.\\nKey Points:\\n1.Range gives a quick sense of dispersion: If the range is small, it indicates that the data \\npoints are close to each other. A larger range suggests that the data points are more spread \\nout.\\n2.Range is sensitive to outliers: Since the range only looks at the two extreme values \\n(maximum and minimum), any outlier can significantly increase the range, even if the rest of \\nthe data is closely packed.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 332}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nVariance\\nVariance ek statistical measure hai jo data set ki values ke beech ki variability ya \\ndispersion ko quantify karta hai. Yani, yeh batata hai ki data ke individual values \\nmean (average) se kitna door hain, aur yeh data set ka spread kitna hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 333}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPopulation Variance and Sample Variance are measures of dispersion that \\nquantify how much data points differ from the mean.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 334}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nStandard Deviation\\nStandard Deviation ek important measure of dispersion hai statistics mein. Yeh batata hai ki aapke data points average \\nke aas-paas kitna spread (faila) hue hain. Simple terms mein, standard deviation se aapko pata chalta hai ki aapke data \\nvalues mean (average) se kitni door ya paas hain.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 335}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question- 1\\nWhich measure of dispersion is affected the least by \\noutliers?\\na) Range\\nb) Variance\\nc) Standard Deviation\\nd) Median'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 336}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question- 2\\nWhich of the following statements is true about the standard deviation?\\na) It can never be zero\\nb) It is always larger than the range\\nc) It is the square root of the variance\\nd) It is less informative than the variance'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 337}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question- 3\\nIf a data set has a range of 30 and a standard deviation of 6, what can you infer about \\nthe data?\\na) The standard deviation is greater than the range\\nb) The range is likely to be larger than the standard deviation\\nc) The data set is normally distributed\\nd) The variance is 36'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 338}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nData Distribution\\nNormal Distribution (Gaussian Distribution)\\nYe distribution bell-shaped hoti hai, jahan data ka majority center ke aas-paas concentrated hota hai aur \\ngradually decrease hota hai dono taraf. Iska mean, median, aur mode sab ek hi point par hota hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 339}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nData Distribution\\nSkewed Distribution\\nSkewness ek statistical measure hai jo data distribution ki symmetry ko describe karta hai. Iska use distribution ke shape \\nko samajhne ke liye kiya jata hai. Skewness ko positive, negative, ya zero ke roop me categorize kiya jata hai.\\nPositive Skewness \\n(Right-Skewed)\\nNegative Skewness\\n(Left-Skewed)'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 340}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nData Distribution\\nUniform Distribution\\nIsme sabhi values ki probability equal hoti hai. Graph ek straight horizontal line hoti hai jo indicate karti \\nhai ki kisi bhi value ki occurrence equal chance ke saath hoti hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 341}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nData Distribution\\nBimodal Distribution\\nBimodal Distribution ek statistical distribution hai jisme data ke do \\ndistinct peaks ya modes hote hain. Iska matlab hai ki data do alag-\\nalag clusters ya groups me divided hota hai, aur in clusters ki \\nfrequencies alag-alag peaks ki form me show hoti hain.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 342}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nData Distribution\\nMultimodal Distribution ek statistical distribution hai \\njisme data ke do se zyada distinct peaks ya modes hote \\nhain. Ye distribution complex data sets ko represent \\nkarta hai jahan data multiple distinct groups ya clusters \\nme divided hota hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 343}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nInferential Statistics me \"estimate\" ka matlab hota hai kisi population parameter \\n(jaise population ka mean ya proportion) ko ek sample data ke basis pe approximate \\nkarna. Jab bhi hum kisi bade group (population) ke baare me kuch conclude karte \\nhain sample data ke use se, to usse \"estimation\" kehte hain.\\nTypes of Estimates in Inferential Statistics:\\nPoint Estimate\\nInterval Estimate\\nEstimate'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 344}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nTypes of Estimates\\nPoint Estimate:\\nDefinition: Point estimate ek single value hoti hai jo sample data se kisi population \\nparameter ka best guess hoti hai.\\nExample: Agar aapke sample ka mean 50 hai, toh aapka point estimate population \\nmean ke liye 50 hoga.\\nInterval Estimate:\\nDefinition: Interval estimate ek range provide karta hai jismein population parameter \\nhone ki probability hoti hai. Yeh zyada reliable hota hai kyunki yeh ek range provide \\nkarta hai, na ki ek single value.\\nExample: Agar aapke sample data se aapka interval estimate 45 se 55 hai, toh aap keh \\nsakte hain ki population mean 45 se 55 ke beech ho sakta hai with a certain level of \\nconfidence.\\nEstimate'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 345}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nConfidence Interval (CI) ek range hota hai jo estimate karta hai ki \\nkisi population parameter ki value kis range ke andar fall kar sakti \\nhai, aur yeh ek confidence level ke sath hota hai. Confidence \\nlevel yeh batata hai ki agar aap multiple samples lenge aur unke \\nconfidence intervals calculate karenge, toh usme se kitne \\nintervals population parameter ko cover karenge.\\nFor Example:\\nAgar aapke sample mean ke liye 95% confidence interval 45 se 55 \\nhai, iska matlab hai ki aapke population mean ka 95% chance hai \\nki yeh range (45 se 55) ke andar hoga.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 346}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nHypothesis Testing \\ninferential statistics mein ek fundamental method hai jo help karta hai data ke basis pe \\ndecisions lene aur conclusions draw karne mein. Yeh process decide karta hai ki sample \\ndata ke basis pe population ke baare mein koi specific claim ya hypothesis true hai ya nahi.\\nHypothesis Testing Kya Hai?\\nHypothesis Testing ek systematic method hai jisme hum ek hypothesis (assumption) ko \\ntest karte hain aur decide karte hain ki sample data us hypothesis ko support karta hai ya \\nnahi. Yeh statistical inference ka ek part hai jo ki probability theory pe based hota hai.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 347}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nHypothesis Testing Mechanism\\n1) Null Hypothesis (H0)\\nThe assumptions you are beginning with \\n2) Alternative Hypothesis (H1)\\nOpposite of Null Hypothesis\\n3) Experiments\\nUse Statistical methods (such as t-tests, z-tests, ANOVA, chi-square tests,etc) to analyze the \\ndata.\\n4)Accept the null hypothesis or reject the null hypothesis\\nIt helps researchers and analysts assess the validity of claims, evaluate the effectiveness of  \\ninterventions and draw meaningful conclusions about population'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 348}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\np-Value Test inferential statistics mein ek key concept hai jo hypothesis testing ke process ka essential \\npart hota hai. Yeh ek measure hai jo batata hai ki sample data ko null hypothesis ke saath kitna \\nconsistent hai. Specifically, p-value se yeh assess kiya jata hai ki null hypothesis ko reject karne ke liye \\naapke sample data ke basis pe kitni evidence hai.\\np-Value Kya Hai?\\np-Value ek probability hai jo aapke sample data ya usse extreme results aane ki probability ko represent \\nkarta hai, assuming ki null hypothesis sach hai. Yeh batata hai ki aapke observed results (ya aur extreme \\nresults) ko observe karna kitna unlikely hai agar null hypothesis sach hoti.\\np-Value Test'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 349}, page_content=\"Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\np-Value Test\\nIn statistics, a t-test is a hypothesis test used to determine if there \\nis a significant difference between the means of two groups. It's \\nespecially useful when dealing with small sample sizes or when \\nthe population standard deviation is unknown. Here’s a \\nbreakdown of what a t-test involves:\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 350}, page_content=\"Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nT Test\\nIn statistics, a t-test is a hypothesis test used to determine if there \\nis a significant difference between the means of two groups. It's \\nespecially useful when dealing with small sample sizes or when \\nthe population standard deviation is unknown.\"),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 351}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nZ - Test\\nZ-Value Test (Z-Test) inferential statistics ka ek method hota hai, jo tab use hota hai jab \\naapko test karna ho ki sample ka mean population mean ke barabar hai ya nahi. Z-test ko \\ntab use kiya jata hai jab sample size bada ho (usually n>30n > 30n>30) ya jab population \\nka standard deviation σ\\\\sigmaσ pata ho.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 352}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nInferential Statistics\\nZ - Test\\nThe average height of all the residents in a city is 168 cm, with a standard deviation = 3.9. A \\ndoctor believes the mean to be different. He measured the height of 36 individuals and found \\nthe average height to be 169.5 cm.\\n1) State null and alternate hypothesis\\n2) At a 95% confidence level, is there enough evidence to reject the null hypothesis'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 353}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question – 1\\nWhat is the purpose of a confidence interval in statistics?\\nA. To determine the exact value of a population parameter.\\nB. To provide a range of values within which the population parameter is expected to \\nlie with a certain level of confidence.\\nC. To calculate the probability of a Type II error.\\nD. To test the null hypothesis.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 354}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question – 2\\nWhich of the following is true about a z-test?\\nA. It is used when the population standard deviation is unknown.\\nB. It is used for hypothesis testing when the sample size is small and the population \\nvariance is known.\\nC. It is appropriate when the sample size is large and the population standard deviation \\nis known.\\nD. It is used to test the relationship between two categorical variables.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 355}, page_content='Website –  www.theiscale.com       Contact : 7880-113-112         theiscale       theiscale.founders \\nPractice Question – 3\\nIf the sample mean is significantly different from the population mean based \\non a z-test, what can be inferred?\\nA. The sample is not representative of the population.\\nB. The null hypothesis can be rejected, suggesting a significant difference.\\nC. The sample size is too small for the z-test.\\nD. The population variance is not known.'),\n",
       " Document(metadata={'producer': 'iLovePDF', 'creator': '', 'creationdate': '', 'source': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'file_path': '../data/pdf/AIEngineer.pdf', 'total_pages': 529, 'format': 'PDF 1.7', 'title': '', 'author': '', 'subject': '', 'keywords': '', 'moddate': '2026-06-17T05:56:46+00:00', 'trapped': '', 'modDate': 'D:20260617055646Z', 'creationDate': '', 'page': 356}, page_content='How to connect with us?\\nWebsite –  www.theiscale.com          Contact : 7880-113-112            theiscale           theiscale.founders \\ntheiscale \\ntheiscale.founders \\nInstagram Handle\\nSiblings - Nishant Dhote & Swati Dhote \\nThe iScale Organization Handle'),\n",
